From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:46:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gfx: JIHAD_GPU_DRAG565=1 composes and reads frames as RGB565
 during a drag (T-637)

The owner, 2026-11-11: 565 during drags only, full colour at rest. On the TouchPad a
565 target draws in 7.6 ms against 14.5 and reads natively in 6.8 ms against 16.6 plus
the swizzle (gpu-bench section 19).

- Each 8888 target gets a lazily made 565 twin of the same size. BeginFrame composes
  into the twin while the daemon reports a drag (jihad_gpu_drag565).
- JihadRead565 reads GL_RGB/UNSIGNED_SHORT_5_6_5 and widens it with NEON to BGRA,
  alpha 0xFF, row flip folded in, into the same shared slot.
- On the window targets only a whole-frame composite changes side.
- Alpha-keeping frames, the read thread and the PASS texture target are never 565.
- jihad_gpu_drag565_frames lets the daemon repaint whole in 8888 when the drag ends.
- Unset: nothing runs; =0 prints the totals line only (the control arm).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
